# English Lessons Web — Project Conventions

Work inside `project/` only. `default/` is the print/PDF reference — do not edit it for web.

## Structure

- `index.html` — lesson library home page
- `lessons/<slug>/index.html` — one self-contained lesson page per slug
- `src/data/lessons.json` — lesson registry (metadata for home page)
- `src/styles/` — shared CSS (tokens, base, lesson)
- `vite.config.js` — auto-discovers lesson folders for build

## Commands

```bash
npm install
npm run dev      # local dev server
npm run build    # static output in dist/
npm run preview  # preview production build
```

## Deployment

Build produces static files in `dist/`. Deploy to any static host (Netlify, Vercel, GitHub Pages, Cloudflare Pages).

- `base: "./"` in production — relative paths work on subpaths and GitHub Pages.
- No server runtime required.

## Future interactivity

- Add behaviour in `src/scripts/` as ES modules.
- Prefer progressive enhancement: lesson readable without JS.
- Interactive widgets (inputs, reveal answers, timers) should use shared classes and data attributes, not inline styles.

## New lesson checklist

- [ ] `lessons/<slug>/index.html` created
- [ ] Entry added to `src/data/lessons.json`
- [ ] Follows 6-section lesson structure (see english-lesson-authoring rule)
- [ ] Responsive at 320px–1280px
- [ ] `npm run build` passes
